+\begin{statement}{B.14}{Proved}{Integral symmetry lifting at every prime}
+For every prime $p$, each homogeneous $S_3$-invariant
+integral special outer leading term lifts to an actual
+$S_3$-centralizing special outer automorphism of the free
+pro-$p$ tripod group, with multiplier one. In particular
+the specified $q_7$, $2q_7$, and $3q_7$ have infinite
+pro-$2$ and pro-$3$ lifts without further rescaling.
+Their first nonzero pentagon defect persists, so these
+lifts satisfy the two cycles and fail the pentagon.
+\end{statement}
+\begin{proof}
+B.14d proves the uniform integral $H^1$ vanishing and
+the convergent symmetry correction at $2$ and $3$.
+B.12 proves the assertion for all other primes.
+The first pentagon coefficient of $m q_7$ is $16m$,
+which is nonzero in every $\mathbb Z_p$ for $m=1,2,3$.
+\end{proof}
+\paragraph{Earlier attacks and the uniform resolution.}
+B.11 does lift each vector without the symmetry condition.
+The first attempted symmetry argument, coprime
+nonabelian $H^1$ vanishing, fails because $6$ is not
+invertible. We replaced this argument by the full
+normalized-bar calculation B.13, which records the
+characteristic-$p$ cohomology. Those modular groups must
+not be identified with the integral $H^1$ obstruction:
+B.14c proves that the latter vanishes in every displayed
+degree at both exceptional primes. The supplied rational class-twelve jet was also
+examined: its displayed weight-nine and weight-eleven
+coefficients have denominators divisible by $2$ and
+$3$ (common denominators $720$ and $8640$).
+Those rational coordinates alone neither give an
+integral group element nor prove that a different
+integral jet cannot exist. Multiplying its first
+term by a prime is not a proof that every subsequent
+obstruction is killed.
+
+We then solved the genuine integral Hall-coordinate
+equations simultaneously, preserving all free parameters
+from earlier degrees. The resulting integral group word
+exists through class fourteen, without scaling $q_7$;
+B.14a and B.14b give the complete certificates.
+These finite certificates were obtained before the
+uniform argument and remain independent checks.
+A finite jet alone would not justify an infinite lift;
+the all-degree integral cohomology calculation and
+actual group convergence in B.14d supply the required
+induction. Assembling separate pro-$p$ lifts into one
+full profinite lift is a distinct question.
