+\begin{statement}{E.14}{Proved}{All marked braid quotients through order one thousand}
+There are exactly $1946$ normal subgroups $K\triangleleft B_3$ with
+$[B_3:K]\leq1000$: $1000$ cyclic quotient kernels and $946$
+noncyclic quotient kernels. Exactly $471$ are contained in $PB_3$.
+For every noncyclic quotient $Q=B_3/K$, put
+\[
+ X=a^2,\quad Y=b^2,\quad Z=ba^2b^{-1},\quad C=(ab)^3= XZY,
+ \quad H=\langle X,Y\rangle,
+ \quad n=\operatorname{lcm}(|X|,|C|).
+\]
+The executed audit lists every pair
+\[
+ m\in\mathbb Z/n,\quad \gcd(2m+1,n)=1,
+ \qquad f\in H'
+\]
+satisfying the two braid hexagons and surjectivity on $H$.
+It obtains the following counts, all of which count pairs:
+\[
+\begin{array}{l|r}
+\text{noncyclic candidate pairs}&255167\\
+\text{both hexagons}&100055\\
+\text{both hexagons and surjectivity on }H&89721\\
+\text{among these, source kernel equals target kernel}&72251\\
+\text{gentle shadows on the }471\text{ eligible kernels}&19147.
